# What the build context must not carry. ADR 0019.
#
# This file is a correctness concern before it is a speed one. `.venv` is the
# clearest case: the build stage creates `/app/.venv` itself, and a local one
# copied in would be a virtual environment built against *this* machine's
# interpreter, silently shadowing the one `uv sync` produced. A `.env` is worse —
# it would bake a developer's database password into a layer.
#
# Deny-by-default was considered and rejected: `*` followed by `!` exceptions is
# safer against a future file nobody thought about, but it makes the list of what
# the image *contains* implicit, and the Dockerfile already copies only the four
# paths it needs. An explicit deny list says what is dangerous; that is the part
# a reader needs to know.

# Would shadow the environment the build stage creates.
.venv/
venv/

# Would bake a developer's secrets into a layer.
.env
.env.*

# Nothing in the image reads history, and it is the largest thing here.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Bytecode and caches, all regenerable and none of it portable.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The test suite does not run in the runtime image: ADR 0011 has the integration
# tests starting their own containers, which a container cannot do for itself.
tests/

# Documentation. The ADRs are the reason this repository is worth reading and
# none of them is read at runtime.
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and operating-system noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# This file and the Dockerfile itself.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
